{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "GIAM (Global Identity and Access Management)",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "\n## Overview\n\nGIAM is the identity authority for **people and systems equally**: employees, customers,\nmicroservices, applications, AI agents and workloads. It is industry neutral, so nothing in its\nmodel, its API or its policy vocabulary names a business concept belonging to the applications it\nprotects.\n\nIt is an identity **broker** as well as an authority: an application speaks one protocol (OIDC) to\none issuer, and GIAM federates behind that to an upstream provider, several at once if needed. Adding\none is a configuration record, not a change in any application.\n\n## How to read this document\n\nEvery operation declares its category:\n\n| Category | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Standard-defined** | Implements a published specification verbatim. The description cites the RFC or specification clause. The error shape is the specification's own, never a house envelope. |\n| **No applicable standard** | Plain REST: plural resources, correct verb semantics, `PATCH` for partial updates, RFC 9457 `application/problem+json` errors, `ETag` and `If-Match` on mutable resources, cursor pagination, `Idempotency-Key` on unsafe operations. |\n\nPublic protocol endpoints live under a realm's issuer path; administrative ones live under\n`/admin/`, so a reader can tell them apart from the URL alone.\n\n## Realms\n\nA realm is a trust and key boundary: its own issuer, its own signing keys, its own JWKS. A token\nminted in one realm is refused by another, which is what makes an institutional boundary real rather\nthan declared. A tenant is a data boundary INSIDE a realm.\n\n## Token validation\n\nBoth models are supported and the choice belongs to the resource server, per operation:\n\n- **Decentralised.** Verification uses only the public keys GIAM publishes, downloaded and cached by\n  the client. No secret at the client, no network call per request, and a GIAM outage does not\n  invalidate an already-issued token.\n- **Centralised.** Introspection at GIAM, so revocation is immediate and the answer reflects current\n  account status rather than what was true at issuance.\n\nThe recommended default is to verify locally on every request and introspect only where the decision\nis expensive to get wrong.\n"
  },
  "components": {
    "securitySchemes": {
      "bearerAuth": {
        "type": "http",
        "scheme": "bearer",
        "bearerFormat": "JWT"
      },
      "clientBasic": {
        "type": "http",
        "scheme": "basic"
      },
      "mtls": {
        "type": "mutualTLS"
      }
    },
    "schemas": {
      "def-0": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "RFC 9457 problem details.",
        "required": [
          "type",
          "title",
          "status"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": true,
        "properties": {
          "type": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "A URI identifying the problem type.",
            "example": "about:blank"
          },
          "title": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "A short, human-readable summary.",
            "example": "Not Found"
          },
          "status": {
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "The HTTP status code.",
            "example": 404
          },
          "detail": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "An explanation specific to this occurrence."
          },
          "instance": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "A URI identifying this occurrence."
          }
        },
        "title": "Problem",
        "example": {
          "type": "about:blank",
          "title": "Not Found",
          "status": 404
        }
      },
      "def-1": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "RFC 6749 section 5.2 error response.",
        "required": [
          "error"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": true,
        "properties": {
          "error": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The RFC 6749 error code.",
            "example": "invalid_request"
          },
          "error_description": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Human-readable detail."
          },
          "error_uri": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "A page describing the error."
          }
        },
        "title": "OAuthError",
        "example": {
          "error": "invalid_request",
          "error_description": "grant_type is required"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "paths": {
    "/": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "getRoot",
        "summary": "Redirect to the API documentation",
        "tags": [
          "system"
        ],
        "description": "No applicable standard. Convenience redirect to /doc.",
        "security": [],
        "responses": {
          "302": {
            "description": "Redirect to /doc"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/health": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "getHealth",
        "summary": "Health check (standard alias)",
        "tags": [
          "system"
        ],
        "description": "No applicable standard for the enclosing API; the body follows IETF health+json.",
        "security": [],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Serving.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "description": "Serving.",
                  "type": "object",
                  "additionalProperties": true
                },
                "example": {
                  "status": "pass",
                  "serviceId": "giam",
                  "checks": {}
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "503": {
            "description": "Degraded.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "description": "Degraded.",
                  "type": "object",
                  "additionalProperties": true
                },
                "example": {
                  "status": "fail",
                  "serviceId": "giam",
                  "checks": {}
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
